# Add this line to frontend/.gitignore (create the file if it doesn't exist):

.env

# # This ensures your Supabase URL and anon key never get committed to GitHub.
# The anon key is technically safe for frontend exposure by Supabase's design (it
# respects Row Level Security policies), but it's still good practice to keep
# .env out of version control — and you should NEVER commit a service_role/secret
# key if you ever use one on a backend.